\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The detection paradox. \emph  {Left}: FL-present tenders have \emph  {lower} within-tender bid dispersion (CV 0.57 vs.\ 1.65), causing variance-based screens to classify them as competitive. \emph  {Right}: the same tenders have 6.4\% higher conditional prices. Coordinated cover bidding (Regime~2) defeats dispersion-based detection precisely when coordination is tightest---the setting where a participation-based screen is most valuable.}}{29}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:detection_paradox}{{3}{29}{The detection paradox. \emph {Left}: FL-present tenders have \emph {lower} within-tender bid dispersion (CV 0.57 vs.\ 1.65), causing variance-based screens to classify them as competitive. \emph {Right}: the same tenders have 6.4\% higher conditional prices. Coordinated cover bidding (Regime~2) defeats dispersion-based detection precisely when coordination is tightest---the setting where a participation-based screen is most valuable}{figure.caption.38}{}}
